[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "adr-2609091500-ad-funded-free-inference-on-murakumo"
  :adr/title "murakumo.cloud serves free inference paid for by advertisers, and one auction serves both slots"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-09-09"
  :adr/deciders "owner directive 2026-09-09; agent implementation"
  :adr/supersedes ""
  :adr/related "adr-2607093500-adnet-first-party-ad-network adr-2608096000-ad-revenue-leverage adr-2607302100-four-planes-of-advertising adr-2607093100-x402-per-request-billing adr-2609070400-human-authentication-web3-first adr-2608039000-no-d1-in-decentralised-paths adr-2609051700-foundation-library-constant-factors"
  :adr/context
  "The owner asked for murakumo.cloud to work as a FREE inference service, funded by an ad network built and connected for the purpose, alongside the existing self-host / x402 / provider / USDC-fee surfaces -- and for itonami.cloud Bots to own 出稿 (placement), 配信 (serving) and 閲覧 (viewing) as three separate responsibilities.

Measured before building, because the workspace already held most of this and the skill `ads-operations` exists precisely to stop the 'it is designed, so it must work' misreading:

- `kotoba-lang/adnet` is a complete pure-.cljc ad auction and USDC accrual layer (eligible? / ecpm-micros / select / serve / apply-spend / charge-micros / accrue / balance-micros). It had no publisher wired to it.
- `cloud-itonami/adserver` implements a Worker for it and is NOT live: ads.x402.nexus is NXDOMAIN, `routes` is commented out in wrangler.jsonc, CAMPAIGNS_JSON is \"[]\".
- `cloud-murakumo.ads` IS live at /api/v1/ads/placement, house-only, one slot (go-sidebar) -- and did not use adnet at all. It carried a SECOND ad decision: first approved listing wins, no bid, no pacing, no budget.
- The credits ledger at api.murakumo.cloud is live with real balances and offers POST /infer/spend, /infer/transfer (CACAO-signed, nonce-checked, overdraft-refusing) and /infer/refund.
- ADR-2608096000 already established that third-party display advertising cannot be a profit centre at this inventory, and ranked 'wire adnet to our own publisher' as the highest-leverage step (2.1) with 'expand to third-party ad networks' last (0.4).

What was genuinely missing was one layer: the rule converting an ad impression into an entitlement to run a metered request. Nothing joined the ad rail (which earns USDC) to the metered service (which charges credits)."
  :adr/decision
  "1. adnet.entitlement is the new join, in kotoba-lang/adnet, pure and dep-free. An impression's charge funds one unit of service, or it is refused with a NAMED reason. It owns the four ways an ad-funded tier leaks, so they are decided once rather than at each call site:
   - the house backfill (adnet.core/serve ALWAYS returns a creative; :kind :house means nobody bid, so it funds nothing),
   - the unbillable impression (charge-micros is 0 for an impression on a CPC campaign, so a PAID serve is not evidence of revenue),
   - the replayed view (the caller must present a receipt it already consumed; nil and false both refuse),
   - the sub-unit charge (credit accumulates in micros; one impression is never rounded up to one unit).

2. ONE auction. cloud-murakumo.ads/select-placement now runs adnet.core/serve when campaigns are configured, keeping the approved-listing path only as the no-campaign fallback. A paid campaign outranks a listing, because a listing carries no bid and cannot be billed, so preferring it would decline money that was offered. The live go-sidebar answer is unchanged byte for byte and a test pins those exact bytes.

3. THREE steps on the wire, because the only evidence an ad was rendered arrives after the response that carried it:
     POST /api/v1/free/impression       -> {unit, receipt}   nothing credited
     POST /api/v1/free/view {receipt}   -> {creditedMicros}   receipt spent
     POST /api/v1/free/chat/completions -> inference          balance spent
     GET  /api/v1/free/status           -> availability + WHO funds it
   Splitting them makes the receipt the single-use thing and makes its consumption a write the server performs rather than a claim the client makes.

4. IDENTITY: a viewer is a signed-in DID -- SIWE or passkey, both of which already mint a cloud-murakumo.token chat session (ADR-2609070400's Web3-first policy; no new authentication surface is introduced). Anonymous callers are refused rather than pooled, because the daily cap and balance ceiling are per viewer and a shared bucket makes both decorative.

5. PRICE: one free request costs what one paid request costs -- 10,000 USDC micros, derived from x402-offer/priced-resources rather than chosen, with a test that fails if either lane moves. HOW MANY ADS is therefore derived too: at $4.00 CPM, three views buy one request. :funding-share defaults to 1, so the free tier breaks even against list price and earns nothing; the marginal cost of a request on the owned fleet is NOT measured, so the code refuses to imply a margin it does not know.

6. STORAGE: D1 ACTIONS_DB (migrations/0005_free_tier.sql), the database that already holds siwe_challenges, with the receipt consumed by the same `UPDATE ... WHERE consumed_at_ms IS NULL ... RETURNING`. Workers KV has no compare-and-swap, so a receipt held in KV could be claimed twice concurrently and each claim would mint a free request. free_ledger is append-only; free_balances is a projection (a fold of the ledger) and can be dropped without losing correctness. The advertiser's money is not in D1 at all: deposits are on-chain via treasury, and campaign spend is recomputable from the receipt rows. This is inside ADR-2608039000's line -- an application quota ledger, not a path claiming decentralisation.

7. BOOTSTRAP (owner choice 2026-09-09): with no advertisers, the tier runs on a DECLARED house sponsorship rather than being switched off, bounded by a FLEET-WIDE daily budget queried from the ledger. GET /api/v1/free/status reports fundingSource 'house-sponsorship' and advertiserFunded 0, and funding-mix keeps sponsored micros out of the advertiser-revenue column -- reporting :advertiser-share as nil with no records rather than 0%, because an unmeasured mix and an all-sponsored one are different states.

8. THREE BOTS, in network-awai/loop-yakuwari (yakuwari/cloud-murakumo.edn): :ad-placement (出稿, advertiser desk), :ad-serving (配信, delivery), :ad-audience (閲覧, audience integrity). Three because 出稿 wants more spend and 閲覧 is the role that reports the spend did not materialise; one Bot holding both would audit its own work. :campaign.register is :approval-required for 出稿 and :blocked for the other two. :funds.move and :pricing.change are :blocked for all three."
  :adr/consequences
  "LIVE and measured 2026-09-09 after deploy (version 9ebd5df7-e240-450e-8876-641d328f4244):
- GET /api/v1/free/status -> available true, fundingSource 'house-sponsorship', advertiserFunded 0, storeReady true, dailyUnitCap 5, unitPriceMicros 10000.
- POST /api/v1/free/impression anonymous -> 401 viewer/not-signed-in.
- /api/v1/ads/placement?placement=go-sidebar&locale=en -> byte-identical to before the auction rewire.
- The free-tier slot exists and answers; the paid /api/v1/messages lane still 401s.
- D1: free_receipts, free_ledger, free_balances present on the remote database.

NOT verified: the authenticated flow past sign-in was exercised only against the built Worker bundle (12 e2e groups over real SQLite running the migration), not against the live deployment, because minting a session token needs MURAKUMO_TOKEN_SECRET and it is NOT in kagi under MURAKUMO_CLOUD_SITE_TOKEN_SECRET_2, the name scripts/deploy-model-hosting-locked.mjs documents. That absence also forced the deploy to run with --bootstrap (main-inclusion assertion kept, concurrency lease skipped). Storing that secret under the documented name is the next concrete step; until then this gap is UNMEASURED, not passing.

Two bugs the e2e test caught that reading did not:
- forwarding reused the original Request, whose body the lane had already read; a Request body reads once, so every free request 502'd looking like an upstream outage.
- the lane forwarded to the anthropic provider, which this deployment does not configure -- the same mistake x402-offer documents after a PAID request 500'd on it in July.

One correctness bug found by re-reading my own field name: :daily-micros was consulted only as (min daily-micros unit-price), making it a per-VIEW cap and never a budget. The per-viewer cap bounds one viewer, so house spend was bounded only by how many viewers turned up. It is now a fleet-wide daily budget and an unreadable figure refuses rather than reading as empty.

One test that could not see what it existed to catch: the first e2e harness hand-rolled the D1 WHERE logic in JavaScript and kept passing after `AND consumed_at_ms IS NULL` and `AND viewer = ?` were deleted from the source. It now runs real SQLite over migrations/0005_free_tier.sql. Writing the warning into the file's own header comment did not implement the warning.

Refused deliberately: POST /events on api.murakumo.cloud as the ledger's home. Measured 2026-09-09, that route is ungated -- the write gate covers /infer/runs, /infer/spend, /infer/transfer and the operator routes and nothing else -- so anyone could append a credit for themselves. An append-only feed anyone may append to is not evidence. That ungated write route is a finding about api.murakumo.cloud, not about this lane.

Not done: cloud-itonami/adserver is still unrouted with an empty campaign registry and was deliberately left that way. The publisher wired to adnet is murakumo's own live Worker, which is ADR-2608096000's step 2.1; standing up a second hostname would have been step 0.4.

North Star: house sponsorship is NOT external revenue. The number that matters is the advertiser-funded share, it starts at 0, and 閲覧 reports it."
